From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: aenertia <aenertia@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 01 Apr 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dsi: reset controller on FIFO and timeout errors

The dsi_err_worker only calls dsi_sw_reset() for MDP FIFO underflow
(status bit 0x8). Plain FIFO errors (0x4) and timeout errors (0x1),
which occur when DCS commands collide with the video data stream,
leave the DSI controller in a permanently stuck state.

On the Retroid Pocket 5 (SM8250) with the CH13726A AMOLED panel,
changing brightness triggers dsi_err_worker with status=0x5
(TIMEOUT|FIFO). Without a reset, the display freezes while the
system remains responsive over SSH.

Extend the reset condition to cover any FIFO error or timeout,
not just MDP FIFO underflow.

Signed-off-by: aenertia <aenertia@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_host.c | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff -rupbN linux.orig/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_host.c linux/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_host.c
--- linux.orig/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_host.c
+++ linux/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_host.c
@@ -1553,8 +1553,11 @@ static void dsi_err_worker(struct work_s
 	u32 status = msm_host->err_work_state;
 
 	pr_err_ratelimited("%s: status=%x\n", __func__, status);
-	if (status & DSI_ERR_STATE_MDP_FIFO_UNDERFLOW)
+	/* Reset on any FIFO or timeout error, not just MDP FIFO underflow.
+	 * Plain FIFO errors (status=0x5: TIMEOUT|FIFO) from DCS commands
+	 * during video mode can leave the controller permanently stuck. */
+	if (status & (DSI_ERR_STATE_MDP_FIFO_UNDERFLOW |
+		      DSI_ERR_STATE_FIFO | DSI_ERR_STATE_TIMEOUT))
 		dsi_sw_reset(msm_host);
 
 	/* It is safe to clear here because error irq is disabled. */
